  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Tuesday)\nIssued at 156 PM MDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\n19z surface analysis had high over the Great Lakes with a warm \nfront from central MT into eastern CO. Modestly tight pressure \ngradient inbetween promoting southeasterly wind gusts into the 30s\non the western SD plains this afternoon. Few shra/TS crawling \nacross south-central SD under weak theta-e advection regime. Water\nvapour loop had upper ridge from TX into eastern WY with upper \nlow near KSLC. Effect of this system main forecast concern.\n\nTonight/Wednesday, upper low lifts northeast as it opens up over \nWY/MT. Stronger low level jet develops ahead of it tonight \ncreating weak buoyancy (<1KJ/kg MUCAPE) in modest low level \ntheta-e advection regime. Result will be some shra/TS lifting \nnortheast across the area into Wednesday. Upslope component to low\nlevel flow may support some fog in/near Black Hills/adjacent \nplains overnight. Temperatures will be near guidance as low clouds\nslowly scour out east of the Black Hills Wednesday afternoon per \nmovement of warm front.\n\nThursday into early next week, southwest flow aloft will persist \nwith periodic frontal passages/shortwaves/downslope flow. Warming\ntrend expected with ensembles in relatively good agreement for \ntemperatures (5-10F spreads). Each wiggle will bring PoPs, but \nthere will be plenty of dry hours ahead of most folks.",
